      "writtenOn": "2025-07-11T18:25:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This shouldn\u0027t be something we support. First valid sampler could be quite surprising, and if we are hitting an unallocated dynamic sampler, I think it means there is an outstanding bug around handling of SkTileMode::kDecal at a higher level.\n\nI suspect what is happening is that KeyHelpers checks for `clampToBorder()` support and switches to shader tiling, but is still using the original `SamplerDesc` when it adds the texture+sampler to the pipeline data gatherer.\n\nInstead of hacking DawnSampler to adjust its keys and having GlobalCache fall back to something else, lets have KeyHelpers switch the SamplerDesc to use SkTileMode::kClamp when it uses shader tiling.  Then we should assert at lower levels that if clamp-to-border is not supported that we aren\u0027t trying to even create a Sampler that would use clamp-to-border.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 133,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 144,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "0d8409c8b8ef91775d2679bbeeb4ee519e02a85f",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
